/* The single source of truth for the backend's named refusal / verdict
   vocabulary (FABLE_GOES_BURR.md item #1; the anchor audit is
   AUDIT-cost-model-refusals.md section 1.6).

   One row per name:

     RVTT_REFUSAL (ENUM_ID, "name-string", "one-line provenance/contract")

   Rules of the table:

   - APPEND-ONLY.  The name strings are frozen API: the twin testsuite
     pins them in dump scans and the board's dump-mining tooling keys on
     them.  Never rename or delete a row; a retired mechanism keeps its
     rows (they simply stop firing).
   - Names are lowercase hyphenated, mechanism-prefixed, dump-stable
     (see FABLE_GOES_BURR.md section 0.3).
   - Uniqueness of ENUM_ID is a compile-time fact (duplicate = build
     break via the enum); uniqueness of the name string is checked by
     the rvtt-refusals.txt catalogue rule in t-riscv-tt.
   - The catalogue rvtt-refusals.txt is GENERATED from this table by
     the build; the 87-reason refusal catalogue class of artifact is
     derived, never re-derived by hand (the laneJC lesson).
   - The third column is a one-line provenance note seeded by the
     mechanical laneJQ census of the pin-48 fprintf sites: the census
     tag (reason = literal in refusal-helper call/return/reason-carrier
     position; dump = named in a refusal-shaped dump message; composed
     = full spelling of a prefix+%s assembled name) plus the file the
     name was first seen in.  Rows added after item #1 should carry a
     real one-line contract instead.

   Emission goes through tt/rvtt-refuse.h; see there for the dual
   legacy-dump / -fopt-info routing contract.  */

RVTT_REFUSAL (ALL_LANES_PROOF_MISSING,
